# Target C: close D=-2,p=5 by a face-local span bound

Date: 2026-09-25

This note closes the remaining h=5 part of the five-singleton profile in the eight-no-root k=5,D=-2,d_root=0,p=5 branch.

Let T be the touched triangle blocks, S the five touched singleton blocks, and C=T\S the touched complete blocks. Since d_root=0, H(C) is independent, so rank H(C)=|T|-5.

Face-local span lemma. For a no-root four-cycle e on support F, temporarily complete its four touched triangle blocks and use the canonical complete-block corrections to cancel its local quotient coordinates. Let tau(e) be the residual 15-dimensional relation row. An independent exact reconstruction of the current-main K8 coordinate normal form checked all 105 no-root four-cycles and found

tau(e) in span_Q{H_b : b is a triangular face of F}.

Each such four-face H-set has exact rational rank three.

For an arbitrary external coefficient relation, summing these canonical cycle corrections puts the residual in H(T). At a singleton block b, replacing the canonical complete correction by the actual singleton correction preserves the local quotient cancellation, so their difference lies in the one-dimensional kernel of the local three-root-cycle quotient map, generated by H_b. Hence every actual external relation row lies in H(T).

Write nu(T)=|T|-rank H(T). The eight no-root cycles use at least three distinct four-supports, because one support has only three no-root orientations. Choose three distinct supports. Their signed tetrahedron boundaries are three independent vectors in ker H(T): any tetrahedron shares at most one triangular face with each of the other two, leaving at least two faces unique to it, so a linear relation forces its coefficient to vanish. Thus nu(T)>=3.

Therefore the touched external rank increment satisfies

r_ext <= rank H(T)-rank H(C)
      = (|T|-nu(T))-(|T|-5)
      = 5-nu(T)
      <= 2.

But the established D=-2,d_root=0,p=5 saturation identity requires external increment exactly five. Contradiction. Thus the full h=5 five-singleton residual is empty.

Current main already closes h=3 and h=4 in the five-singleton profile and closes the separate (s,t)=(3,1) three-singleton-plus-pair profile. The three-generator reduction proves those are the only two incomplete-root profiles. Therefore the entire eight-no-root k=5,D=-2,(d_root,p)=(0,5) arithmetic branch is empty.

The remaining k=5 arithmetic branch is D=-1,(d_root,p)=(0,6).

Validation: the 105-cycle face-local identity was executed in exact rational arithmetic in an independent reconstruction of the committed normal form. No modular rank computation is used in the new lemma.